"""Generate stub bodies for external functions with a large language model.

This module implements the ``ikos-api-spec`` command line tool, the middle
stage of the spec pipeline: ``ikos-api-census`` lists the unmodeled external
functions, this tool writes stub bodies for them, and ``ikos-stub link``
assembles program bitcode with the stub library into one analyzable module.

The v1 design is *fully LLM-based*: every semantic decision -- which
``__ikos_*`` helpers to call, what preconditions to check, which buffers to
havoc, what the return value can be -- comes from the model.  Everything
that must not be left to chance stays deterministic:

* the C signature and struct typedefs are rendered from the IR ``declare``
  line by ``ikos-stub``'s scaffold machinery, and the model fills in only
  the body, which is spliced between the signature and the closing brace;
* every candidate is compiled with the ikos clang flags and its compiled
  signature key is compared against the program declaration before it is
  installed into the stub library;
* a never-returning function (by name or by the ``noreturn`` attribute of
  its declare line) must end its body in ``__ikos_assume(0)``, and
  special-control-flow functions (setjmp/longjmp, the C++ exception
  runtime) are refused outright instead of being modeled;
* every candidate is also analyzed on its own -- ikos over a driver that
  feeds each parameter full nondeterminism -- and a definite error
  located inside the stub file itself rejects the body;
* a candidate rejected by the lexical guard, the compiler, the signature
  gate or the stub self-check is fed back to the model for up to
  ``--max-retries`` repair rounds.

The tool is a standalone script: it is not wired into the analyzer CMake
build.  It locates the installed ikos python package on its own (from
``ikos-stub`` on PATH, or ``--ikos-prefix`` / ``--site-packages``) and
reuses ``ikos.stub`` / ``ikos.api_census`` internals, so its decisions and
skeletons match ``ikos-stub`` exactly.  The LLM endpoint is any
OpenAI-compatible chat completions API: ``--provider openai|deepseek|glm``
selects a built-in preset (base URL, API key environment variable, default
model), or ``--base-url`` / ``--model`` point at any other endpoint; the
client is standard-library only.

Generated files carry a provenance header (``generated by ikos-api-spec``)
that also serves as the ownership mark: the tool never overwrites a stub
file it did not generate itself.

Installed bodies are also recorded in a stub database (``--db-dir``,
default ``~/.cache/ikos-api-spec/stubdb``) keyed by source name +
signature key.  ``generate`` consults it before asking the model, and the
``prefetch`` subcommand installs database hits for a program's missing
external functions with zero LLM calls.

A run can also target the numeric abstract domain of the analysis
(``--domain <name>``, the token of ikos's ``-d`` flag): the default
``all`` keeps every stub sound under every backend (the judge admits by
convex hull AND congruence closure); a concrete domain relaxes the
judge, the game metrics and the prompt guidance to the join families
that backend tracks, and the database stores the body under that domain.

See tool/api-spec/README.md for the documentation.
"""
